                        "content": "The nurse is performing an assessment on a client with a diagnosis of myxedema (hypothyroidism). Which assessment finding would the nurse expect to note in this client?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nMyxedema is a deficiency of thyroid hormone. The client will present with a puffy, edematous face, especially around the eyes (periorbital edema), along with coarse facial features; dry skin; and dry, coarse hair and eyebrows. The remaining options are noted in the client with hyperthyroidism.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nFocus on the subject, manifestations of hypothyroidism. Recalling the function of thyroid hormone and that a deficiency of thyroid hormone occurs in this condition will direct you to the correct option.",
